p":[],"primaryFormat":"physical","personalRating":5,"certifiedSlay":true,"brainChemistry":false,"favorite":false,"goodreadsBookId":"50892338","dateAdded":"2022-02-07","source":"goodreads","createdAt":"2026-10-06T16:56:09.947Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-06T16:56:09.947Z","coverUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/isbn/9781534441606-L.jpg"},"readingRecord":{"id":"goodreads-50892338-read-1","bookId":"goodreads-50892338","status":"completed","readingMethod":"physical","finishedAt":"2025-05-21","rating":5,"certifiedSlay":true,"readingNumber":1,"isReread":false,"progressEntries":[],"createdAt":"2026-10-06T16:56:09.947Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-06T16:56:09.947Z"},"rawShelves":["5-star-reads"],"readCount":1,"wasTbbBuddyRead":false,"review":{"id":"goodreads-review-50892338","bookId":"goodreads-50892338","readingRecordId":"goodreads-50892338-read-1","rating":5,"body":"5/5 Stars – Black Girl Magic Meets Arthurian Legend in the Best Way<br/><br/>Legendborn by Tracy Deonn is a stunning reimagining of fantasy that unapologetically centers a Black girl’s experience in a world where she was never supposed to belong—but absolutely does. From the very first page, this book radiates with power, grief, and resilience wrapped in a story that honors ancestral strength and the richness of Southern Black culture.<br/><br/>Deonn weaves African American history and generational trauma into a narrative that is as magical as it is grounded. The protagonist doesn’t just face supernatural threats—she navigates spaces shaped by privilege, gatekeeping, and erasure, all while carrying the weight of her own loss. Her Blackness isn’t an afterthought—it’s a source of magic, identity, and resistance.<br/><br/>This is the kind of fantasy so many of us have been waiting for: where the magic isn’t just in spells and swords, but in heritage, memory, and the unbreakable ties to the ancestors who walked before us. Legendborn is more than a novel—it’s a reclamation. Bold, brilliant, and beautifully melanated. This 